# Leaf's settings. Copy to .env (cp .env.example .env) and edit; .env is
# gitignored. Every setting is optional except LEAF_DATA. Uncomment a line to
# use it. Details: README.md (Settings) and docs/spec/deployment.md.

# The wiki folder, which must exist (default ~/leaf). run.sh expands a ~.
# Used without run.sh, give an absolute path.
LEAF_DATA=~/leaf

# Timezone, so "today" is your day (default: the host's, via run.sh; else UTC).
# TZ=Europe/Berlin

# Login gate. Sessions survive restarts: Leaf keeps its own key in .leaf/
# (never in git). LEAF_SECRET_KEY sets one instead.
# LEAF_PASSWORD=
# LEAF_SECRET_KEY=

# Turns on /mcp: the bearer token MCP clients send (without it /mcp is off).
# Make one with: openssl rand -hex 32
# LEAF_MCP_TOKEN=

# Users, instead of LEAF_PASSWORD and LEAF_MCP_TOKEN: each signs in with
# their own name and password, and their changes are committed in their
# name. A user's password is kept as a hash; make the line with
# ./run.sh passwd alice. Each user's own MCP token (optional) lets an
# assistant act as them. Each user has private pages (private/<name>/) and
# private deck tasks; the rest of the wiki is shared. See docs/spec/users.md. Names: lowercase letters, digits and hyphens
# (mary-ann's settings are LEAF_USER_MARY_ANN_…).
# LEAF_USERS=alice,bob
# LEAF_USER_ALICE_PASSWORD=pbkdf2-sha256:600000:…
# LEAF_USER_ALICE_MCP_TOKEN=

# A remote for the wiki's git repository.
# LEAF_GIT_REMOTE=git@example.org:you/wiki.git

# Network access: 1 listens on the LAN (e.g. for your phone), default localhost
# only. LEAF_HOSTS names the hosts Leaf may be reached by besides localhost
# (behind a reverse proxy, e.g. wiki.example.org).
# LEAF_ALLOW_REMOTE=1
# LEAF_HOSTS=

# Leaf's address as your browser knows it, for links handed to AI clients.
# LEAF_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5000

# Pages hidden in sharing mode: #tags and folders/ (default #noshare).
# LEAF_NOSHARE=#noshare,people/

# How dates read and the day weeks start on, as a locale tag (default: US
# English dates, weeks from Monday). The UI's words stay English.
# LEAF_LOCALE=de-AT
# iso writes dates as YYYY-MM-DD (ISO 8601); weekday and month names still
# follow LEAF_LOCALE.
# LEAF_DATE_FORMAT=iso

# Semantic search with a local model, baked in at build (adds about 1 GB).
# LEAF_SEMANTIC_SEARCH=on
# How similar a passage must be to count as a match (e.g. 0.4).
# LEAF_SEMANTIC_MIN_SCORE=

# 1 logs each search_wiki query to .leaf/queries.jsonl (for ./run.sh eval).
# LEAF_QUERY_LOG=1

# Only for docker compose without run.sh (run.sh sets these itself):
# LEAF_BIND=0.0.0.0
# LEAF_UID=1000
# LEAF_GID=1000

# compose.nas.yaml (the prebuilt image on a NAS or server) also needs
# LEAF_DATA as an absolute path, LEAF_UID/LEAF_GID of the wiki folder's owner
# and LEAF_HOSTS (or LEAF_ALLOW_REMOTE=1). The port on the host, default 5080
# (Synology's DSM has 5000):
# LEAF_PORT=5080
